  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Systemic availability of the oral solution is low, about 14%. A high-fat meal raises exposure by 23 to 35%, and the drug is about 92% bound to plasma protein.",
    "substance": "A powder, insoluble in water but freely soluble in acetone and chloroform, with a molecular weight of 914.2.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA as an oral solution and as 0.5, 1 and 2 mg tablets, dosed daily.",
    "safety": "Boxed warning for infection and lymphoma risk; use is not recommended in liver or lung transplant patients. Contraindicated in hypersensitivity to the drug; angioedema and exfoliative dermatitis occur.",
    "indication": "Prophylaxis of organ rejection in patients aged 13 years and over receiving kidney transplants, given with cyclosporine and corticosteroids.",
    "mechanism": "Binds FKBP-12 and inhibits the mTOR kinase, blocking T-lymphocyte activation and proliferation; calcineurin is unaffected."
  },
  "tell": "An mTOR inhibitor with a terminal half-life of about 62 hours and a boxed warning on infection and lymphoma.",
